report:
Reading DateTime and decimal values

Hi Debezium Team,
I have a problem with reading both decimals and DateTime values from Debezium. I receive them as base64 strings but they seem to be invalid.
I have value of 100.00 in the database which is sent as "JxA=". From what I know, it is 0x2710 which renders as '\x10 but 10,000 when converted from base64 to base10.
How can I make sure that I correctly read this value? I've tried this approach (in C# reader):
var bytes = Convert.FromBase64String(base64String);
var value = BitConverter.ToDouble(bytes, 0);
return (decimal)value;
And this approach:
var bytes = Convert.FromBase64String(base64String);
var decimalInt = BitConverter.ToInt32(bytes, 0);
return (decimal)decimalInt / 100;
In the second case I receive "The array starting from the specified index is not long enough to read a value of the specified type". The first approach doesn't work either. It means that I cannot read "JxA=".
How should I approach it?
I also understand that I would need to divide by 100 because the original column has decimal(10,2) in MySQL - so I think this 100 relates to 2 zeroes in places after dot in the original column, whereas 10^2 = 100. So my converter would work only if all the columns are decimal(*,2) and obviously I have other columns as well, where the precision may be different.
With DateTime my converter couldn't convert the base64 to DateTime because it was claiming that it is around year 50 000 so above max range of 9999 year (even though I set date from year 2024 in the database by insert).
Any guidelines are very welcome.
Thank you,
Rafal
